2 |     var got = 0
3 |     select {
  |     ^^^^^^ a cancellation here would have nowhere to go
  |
  = note: a cancellation that reaches a blocked `select` runs its `timeout(…)` arm when it has
    one, and otherwise leaves the `select` as the `cancelled` error value of the function,
    as `?` would from a receive [conc.select.ready]. Give the `select` a timeout arm, or
    give the function a row that admits `cancelled` (`-> !T` infers one).
help: make `wait_one` fallible: `! {cancelled}`
  |
1 | fn wait_one(ch: channel[int]) -> int ! {cancelled} {
